ousvibecoding-installed-source-clean-main-followup-01/.worktrees/cached-review-provenance/.svc/external-review-artifacts/cached-review-provenance/run-exec-passing-only/attempt-1-findings.json","sha256":"ae84fd459b6462caf498b901018aedb03b5309f7d7486d130abe7852f178341d"}],"deletion_bearing":false,"parse_collect_evidence":[]},"receipt_type":"review-exec","wi":"WI-CACHED-REVIEW-PROVENANCE-01","timestamp":"2026-09-07T18:49:11.946Z","author_family":"openai","reviewer_family":"xai","target_sha":"22a78dd1a792f625ef3dc609e4b9932d19a2e46a","sha":"22a78dd1a792f625ef3dc609e4b9932d19a2e46a"},"slot::review-plan::WI-CACHED-REVIEW-PROVENANCE-01::22a78dd1a792f625ef3dc609e4b9932d19a2e46a":{"schema_version":3,"tree_hash":"c17a13a97cac8e35563ea4b1001b20cf3bfa06de","candidate_digest":"54ea7414c16c8c2ed29f90be615cf8d8b5f14fce264b65799f9675d2e1dffa93","reviewed_plan_digest":"28f2e5b7eb9d76857875c89d75902ba5b03168162e525ac0d4d0571e922f1eeb","self_review":{"orchestrator":"codex","findings_count":0,"notes":"All367free tier1 checks pass; Sol high PASS on integrated tree; actual signed HoursHub replay and8invalid variants pass. Retrospective plan recovery explicitly disclosed and owner-authorized. No installation or hosted app change claimed."},"adversarial_review":{"primary_reviewer_host":"grok","primary_used":true,"fallback_host":"grok","fallback_used":false,"iteration_count":3,"findings":[{"id":"F-001","severity":"high","claim":"The landing plan mutates GitHub, host installs, and HoursHub state without the required External State coupling section.","analysis":"review-plan Step 1.5 treats a missing `## External State` section as HIGH and blocking. This document never provides that section, nor the allowed substitute line that names the walked taxonomy and untouched environments. The remaining prospective tasks are not repo-local: Tasks 4–6 push a branch, open a PR, and squash-merge; Task 7 runs `./setup --all-hosts` against canonical main; Task 10 edits an HoursHub worktree emitter. Those are host config, remote git, and a second repository. The plan does constrain production, account-multicontext, and staging-fence writes, and it names exact helpers, but constraints in prose are not coupling rows with named wiring. Without the table, install drift, a leftover remote branch/PR, or an HoursHub emitter edit can proceed as undeclared external mutation. Rollback only reverts the five framework files and explicitly does not unwrite issued evidence, so the missing section also leaves the non-repo side effects without a declared recovery path.","evidence":[{"path":".svc/external-review-artifacts/cached-review-provenance/scope-correction.md","sha256":"a7397282a536aab6fb32673237f89c03e6052c34fda008121546c94c68825487"}],"proposed_fix":"Add an `## External State` table before the helper listing with at least these rows: (1) GitHub `s7an-it/serious-serious-vibe-engineering` branch `fix/cached-review-provenance`, PR, and squash merge — coupled — wiring `promote.py push` and `promote.py merge` plus `merge-pr-with-review-receipt.mjs`; recovery is leave the PR closed/deleted by the merge helper or delete the unused remote branch without `--force`. (2) Managed host install trees updated by `./setup --all-hosts` — coupled — wiring `check-install-drift.sh --all-hosts` after ff-only main; recovery is reviewed revert then canonical `./setup --all-hosts` again. (3) HHWT emitter `.svc/external-state/staging-scout-hygiene/emit-recovered-planning-receipts.mjs` — coupled — wiring Task 10 and `test-cache-recovery.mjs`; recovery is stop Scout promotion as already stated. (4) Production app, account-multicontext, and staging fence — decoupled-justified — no writes in this operation, with the existing stop-Scout rule if consumer proof fails. Close with `Untouched environments ...` covering the rest of the 15-entry taxonomy.","disposition":"fixed","justification":"Populated External State table maps actual mutation surfaces, wiring, recovery and all15taxonomy entries. Broad preexisting host drift repair is explicitly excluded; canonical source direct invocation is the actual install target."},{"id":"F-002","severity":"high","claim":"The round-3 review emitter rejects any findings, so it cannot perform the adjudication path this final bounded round requires.","analysis":"This invocation is explicitly the final bounded retrospective plan review (round 3). The protocol terminates after three rounds by disposition: remaining High findings are recorded and the plan can still promote; a fourth launcher round is forbidden. The plan text says emitters refuse only unadjudicated findings and that findings are resolved, hash-bound, and never erased. The embedded `emit-integrated-review.mjs` does not implement that. After requiring verdict `pass` or `pass-with-findings`, it throws if `findings.findings.length` is non-zero and again if any certification has `certified !== true`. There is no dispositions file, bounded-exit object, or pass-with-acks construction. The only envelope this helper can emit is empty `findings` plus all-true certifications. That forces either a rubber-stamp empty review or a forbidden fourth review after fixes. It also cannot land this round honestly if F-001 (or any other finding) is dispositioned rather than deleted. The helper is otherwise correctly fail-closed on raw `fail` and on failed certifications; the defect is the missing hash-bound adjudication path the plan and round-3 cap both claim exists.","evidence":[{"path":".svc/external-review-artifacts/cached-review-provenance/emit-integrated-review.mjs","sha256":"5a5dfbe0d937703a103b5aefad01966c64c6871d24a101c79577c70dd602d2da"},{"path":".svc/external-review-artifacts/cached-review-provenance/scope-correction.md","sha256":"a7397282a536aab6fb32673237f89c03e6052c34fda008121546c94c68825487"}],"proposed_fix":"Keep the supported `git commit -m` argv unchanged. Extend `emit-integrated-review.mjs` so a hash-bound dispositions file is required when `findings.findings.length > 0`: every finding id must have a disposition (`fixed` with candidate-bound proof, or `accept-with-justification` / `reject-with-justification`), raw `findings.json` and `receipt.json` bytes stay in `reviewer_evidence`, and the emitted review receipt uses `pass-with-acks` plus a `bounded_exit` object whose `residual_highs` length equals remaining Highs. Do not throw merely because findings exist. Alternatively, delete the adjudication claim and state that this helper only emits `findings:[]`; in that case F-001 must be fixed in the plan and this round’s findings closed as `fixed` before emission, still without a fourth launcher call.","disposition":"fixed","justification":"Passing-with-findings emitter now requires explicit dispositions and verifies all counter-evidence hashes; raw reviewer findings retained. General bounded-failure generation is not claimed."},{"id":"F-003","severity":"medium","claim":"AC6’s HoursHub emitter update is still not content-complete: Task 10 names receipts but not the command/output hashes or the file rewrite.","analysis":"AC6 is in scope for this landing plan: after install, the installed verifier must accept the real cached HoursHub replay and reject invalid variants, then Scout may resume. Tasks 7–9 give copy-pasteable install and focused eval commands. Task 10 then requires a code change in `emit-recovered-planning-receipts.mjs` to bind the selected replay to its primary source and to the original `reviewer_run` commands and output hashes. The plan inlines replay/source paths and SHA-256 values, plus HoursHub tree and candidate digest, but it does not inline those command/output hashes or the replacement file contents. Inline mode does not require a full blueprint for the already-implemented five-file patch, and an executor can read the named primary source receipt, but the remaining HoursHub edit is still a content gap: the orchestrator has to reconstruct the mapping at execution time. That is the residual rubric-2 miss. It will not block t